    "source": "General MIDI Level 1 Percussion Key Map (MIDI Manufacturers Association, GM1 spec) — the standard channel-10 note assignments, notes 35-81. Verbatim from the published map; the ROLE grouping is Tonality's own coarse vocabulary (several GM notes share a role: three snares-ish, six toms, five crash-class cymbals), chosen so a rhythmic pattern can be stated as 'kick on every beat' rather than as a specific note number. Notes outside 35-81 have no GM percussion meaning and are reported unmapped rather than guessed.",
    "license": "GM1 is a published interoperability specification; the note-name table is factual and not copyrightable as data.",
